ASoC: qcom: sc8280xp: add Xiaomi Marble speaker TDM backend

Marble's two AW88263S speaker amplifiers sit on the tertiary TDM
interface. Stock Android runs it at 96 kHz with 32-bit samples in four
32-bit slots (short frame sync) and holds an LPASS core vote while it is
active ("qcom,mi2s-tdm-is-hw-vote-needed"). The amplifiers' interface
registers come from their ACF profile, which expects that layout.

Add a "xiaomi,marble-sndcard" card with the SM8450 card settings (the
"sm8450" driver name keeps the qcom/sm8450 topology and UCM paths) plus
board fields: the TDM backend rate and sample format applied in the
backend fixup, and a "tdm-vote" clock held from backend startup to
shutdown. Slot layout and bit clock use the 7.3 DAI-node TDM slot
properties and the backend "bclk" clock (a689ee3b2fcd); framing comes
from the topology.

This replaces the qcom,tdm-* card properties and card clocks of
iLtanaka's f5bc71d7372e ("ASoC: qcom: sc8280xp: support TDM backends
and 32-bit slots", https://github.com/iLtanaka/linux-marble), which
predates the 7.3 TDM support.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Source-commit: 7d7791df79cdad82d970bbaccb8f9aa0e3337350
Source-author: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Source-date: 2026-10-25T09:50:08+08:00
Imported-from: pkgs/linux-kernel/sm7475/marble/patches/local/0056-arm64-dts-qcom-sm8475-xiaomi-marble-describe-the-spe.patch

arm64: dts: qcom: sm8475-xiaomi-marble: describe the speaker TDM link for 7.3

Use the Linux 7.3 TDM description for the tertiary TDM speaker link
instead of the qcom,tdm-* card properties and card clocks of the
deferred iLtanaka commit f5bc71d7372e:

- "xiaomi,marble-sndcard" (96 kHz S32_LE TDM backend, LPASS core vote
  through the "tdm-vote" card clock);
- standard DAI TDM slot properties on the CPU endpoint: four 32-bit
  slots, slots 0 and 1 active;
- the backend bit clock (TER_TDM_IBIT) as the "bclk" clock of the
  TERTIARY_TDM_RX_0 backend DAI node.

Framing (short frame sync, one-bit delay, internal sync, data output
enabled) is described by the board topology.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Source-commit: 9360479ef94493e31e3e1d5ccd5004252d79b053
Source-author: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Source-date: 2026-10-25T14:56:55+08:00
Imported-from: pkgs/linux-kernel/sm7475/marble/patches/local/0063-ASoC-qcom-sc8280xp-drive-the-speaker-earpiece-switch.patch

ASoC: qcom: sc8280xp: drive the speaker/earpiece switch to the speaker

On the Xiaomi Poco F5 (marble) the top AW88263S amplifier drives either
the top speaker or the earpiece through an output switch on gpio52,
described by "speaker-earpiece-gpios" (active = earpiece). Nothing
claimed the line, so it stayed a pulled-down input.

Request the optional GPIO at probe as an output driven inactive, routing
the amplifier to the speaker, as iLtanaka's linux-marble does (the card
probe of e21870ba92a9 "ASoC: qcom: sc8280xp: connect Marble handset
voice routes" by Halhadus <eneshakans45@proton.me>,
https://github.com/iLtanaka/linux-marble). The ALSA switch control and
the voice links of that commit are not included.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../bindings/sound/qcom,sm8250.yaml           | 11 +++
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-marble.dts    | 32 +++---
 sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c                     | 99 ++++++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 128 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,sm8250.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,sm8250.yaml
index fa0c38a541..438d552184 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,sm8250.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,sm8250.yaml
@@ -31,6 +31,7 @@ properties:
               - qcom,sm8550-sndcard
               - qcom,sm8650-sndcard
               - qcom,sm8750-sndcard
+              - xiaomi,marble-sndcard
           - const: qcom,sm8450-sndcard
       - enum:
           - ayaneo,pocket-s2-sndcard
@@ -73,6 +74,16 @@ properties:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/string
     description: User visible long sound card name
 
+  clocks:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  clock-names:
+    items:
+      - const: tdm-vote
+    description:
+      LPASS core vote held while a TDM backend is active, for boards whose
+      TDM interface needs it.
+
   speaker-earpiece-gpios:
     maxItems: 1
     description:
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-marble.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-marble.dts
index 1b391d31ee..58f51e5b30 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-marble.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-marble.dts
@@ -1103,8 +1103,9 @@ tx-pins {
 
 /*
  * Speakers: 2x Awinic AW88263S (register compatible with AW88261) on i2c15,
- * fed by the tertiary TDM interface like stock ("TDM-LPAIF-RX-TERTIARY"),
- * framed as I2S (2 x 32-bit slots, BCLK = 64 * fs) as set by the amp ACF.
+ * fed by the tertiary TDM interface like stock ("TDM-LPAIF-RX-TERTIARY"):
+ * 96 kHz, 32-bit samples, 4 x 32-bit slots (slots 0/1 carry the two amps),
+ * short frame sync; the amps' interface registers come from their ACF.
  * 0x34 = top (also the earpiece, see gpio52), 0x35 = bottom. Pins and gpios
  * from the stock device tree.
  */
@@ -1184,8 +1185,19 @@ data1-pins {
 	};
 };
 
+&q6apmbedai {
+	#address-cells = <1>;
+	#size-cells = <0>;
+
+	dai@56 {
+		reg = <TERTIARY_TDM_RX_0>;
+		clocks = <&q6prmcc LPASS_CLK_ID_TER_TDM_IBIT LPASS_CLK_ATTRIBUTE_COUPLE_NO>;
+		clock-names = "bclk";
+	};
+};
+
 &sound {
-	compatible = "qcom,sm8450-sndcard";
+	compatible = "xiaomi,marble-sndcard", "qcom,sm8450-sndcard";
 	model = "SM8475-Xiaomi-Marble";
 	speaker-earpiece-gpios = <&tlmm 52 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 
@@ -1193,15 +1205,8 @@ &sound {
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 
 	/* Stock: qcom,mi2s-tdm-is-hw-vote-needed for the tertiary interface */
-	clocks = <&q6prmcc LPASS_HW_MACRO_VOTE LPASS_CLK_ATTRIBUTE_COUPLE_NO>,
-		 <&q6prmcc LPASS_CLK_ID_TER_TDM_IBIT LPASS_CLK_ATTRIBUTE_COUPLE_NO>;
-	clock-names = "tdm-vote", "tdm-bclk";
-
-	/* Stock speaker TDM: 96 kHz, 4 x 32-bit slots, short frame sync */
-	qcom,tdm-slots = <4>;
-	qcom,tdm-slot-width = <32>;
-	qcom,tdm-rate = <96000>;
-	qcom,tdm-format = "dsp_a";
+	clocks = <&q6prmcc LPASS_HW_MACRO_VOTE LPASS_CLK_ATTRIBUTE_COUPLE_NO>;
+	clock-names = "tdm-vote";
 
 	/* Analog mics on the WCD9385; ADCs feed the TX macro over SoundWire */
 	audio-routing = "AMIC1", "MIC BIAS1",
@@ -1234,6 +1239,9 @@ speaker-dai-link {
 
 		cpu {
 			sound-dai = <&q6apmbedai TERTIARY_TDM_RX_0>;
+			dai-tdm-slot-num = <4>;
+			dai-tdm-slot-width = <32>;
+			dai-tdm-slot-rx-mask = <1 1 0 0>;
 		};
 
 		codec {
diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
index 4d48e1012c..cc7c85bfa8 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
@@ -2,6 +2,8 @@
 // Copyright (c) 2022, Linaro Limited
 
 #include <dt-bindings/sound/qcom,q6afe.h>
+#include <linux/clk.h>
+#include <linux/gpio/consumer.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <sound/soc.h>
@@ -71,6 +73,11 @@ struct qcom_snd_soc_common {
 	bool mi2s_mclk_enable;
 	bool mi2s_bclk_enable;
 	bool wcd_jack;
+	/* TDM backend rate and sample format; 0 keeps 48 kHz S16_LE */
+	unsigned int tdm_rate;
+	snd_pcm_format_t tdm_format;
+	/* TDM backends need an LPASS core vote ("tdm-vote" clock) */
+	bool tdm_hw_vote;
 	int (*snd_prepare)(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream);
 };
 
@@ -80,6 +87,7 @@ struct sc8280xp_snd_data {
 	struct snd_soc_jack jack;
 	struct snd_soc_jack dp_jack[8];
 	const struct qcom_snd_soc_common *priv;
+	struct clk *tdm_vote;
 	bool jack_setup;
 };
 
@@ -218,6 +226,7 @@ static int sc8280xp_snd_init(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd)
 static int sc8280xp_be_hw_params_fixup(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd,
 				     struct snd_pcm_hw_params *params)
 {
+	struct sc8280xp_snd_data *data = snd_soc_card_get_drvdata(rtd->card);
 	struct snd_soc_dai *cpu_dai = snd_soc_rtd_to_cpu(rtd, 0);
 	struct snd_interval *rate = hw_param_interval(params,
 					SNDRV_PCM_HW_PARAM_RATE);
@@ -236,6 +245,14 @@ static int sc8280xp_be_hw_params_fixup(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd,
 	case TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_3:
 		channels->min = 1;
 		break;
+	case PRIMARY_TDM_RX_0 ... QUINARY_TDM_TX_7:
+		if (data->priv->tdm_rate)
+			rate->min = rate->max = data->priv->tdm_rate;
+		if (data->priv->tdm_format) {
+			snd_mask_none(fmt);
+			snd_mask_set_format(fmt, data->priv->tdm_format);
+		}
+		break;
 	default:
 		break;
 	}
@@ -368,9 +385,46 @@ static int sc8280xp_snd_hw_free(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream)
 	return qcom_snd_sdw_hw_free(substream, &data->stream_prepared[cpu_dai->id]);
 }
 
+static bool sc8280xp_is_tdm(struct snd_soc_dai *cpu_dai)
+{
+	return cpu_dai->id >= PRIMARY_TDM_RX_0 && cpu_dai->id <= QUINARY_TDM_TX_7;
+}
+
+static int sc8280xp_snd_startup(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream)
+{
+	struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd = snd_soc_substream_to_rtd(substream);
+	struct snd_soc_dai *cpu_dai = snd_soc_rtd_to_cpu(rtd, 0);
+	struct sc8280xp_snd_data *data = snd_soc_card_get_drvdata(rtd->card);
+	int ret;
+
+	if (sc8280xp_is_tdm(cpu_dai)) {
+		ret = clk_prepare_enable(data->tdm_vote);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}
+
+	ret = qcom_snd_sdw_startup(substream);
+	if (ret && sc8280xp_is_tdm(cpu_dai))
+		clk_disable_unprepare(data->tdm_vote);
+
+	return ret;
+}
+
+static void sc8280xp_snd_shutdown(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream)
+{
+	struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd = snd_soc_substream_to_rtd(substream);
+	struct snd_soc_dai *cpu_dai = snd_soc_rtd_to_cpu(rtd, 0);
+	struct sc8280xp_snd_data *data = snd_soc_card_get_drvdata(rtd->card);
+
+	qcom_snd_sdw_shutdown(substream);
+
+	if (sc8280xp_is_tdm(cpu_dai))
+		clk_disable_unprepare(data->tdm_vote);
+}
+
 static const struct snd_soc_ops sc8280xp_be_ops = {
-	.startup = qcom_snd_sdw_startup,
-	.shutdown = qcom_snd_sdw_shutdown,
+	.startup = sc8280xp_snd_startup,
+	.shutdown = sc8280xp_snd_shutdown,
 	.hw_params = sc8280xp_snd_hw_params,
 	.hw_free = sc8280xp_snd_hw_free,
 	.prepare = sc8280xp_snd_prepare,
@@ -395,6 +449,7 @@ static int sc8280xp_platform_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	struct snd_soc_card *card;
 	struct sc8280xp_snd_data *data;
 	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
+	struct gpio_desc *speaker_earpiece;
 	int ret;
 
 	card = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*card), GFP_KERNEL);
@@ -410,6 +465,23 @@ static int sc8280xp_platform_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (!data->priv)
 		return -ENODEV;
 
+	if (data->priv->tdm_hw_vote) {
+		data->tdm_vote = devm_clk_get(dev, "tdm-vote");
+		if (IS_ERR(data->tdm_vote))
+			return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(data->tdm_vote),
+					     "failed to get tdm-vote clock\n");
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * Speaker/earpiece output switch (Marble: the top amplifier drives
+	 * either the top speaker or the earpiece): select the speaker.
+	 */
+	speaker_earpiece = devm_gpiod_get_optional(dev, "speaker-earpiece",
+						   GPIOD_OUT_LOW);
+	if (IS_ERR(speaker_earpiece))
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(speaker_earpiece),
+				     "failed to get speaker-earpiece GPIO\n");
+
 	card->owner = THIS_MODULE;
 	card->dev = dev;
 	dev_set_drvdata(dev, card);
@@ -518,6 +590,28 @@ static const struct qcom_snd_soc_common sm8450_priv_data = {
 			 SND_SOC_DAIFMT_I2S,
 };
 
+/*
+ * Xiaomi Poco F5 / Redmi Note 12 Turbo (marble): two AW88263S speaker
+ * amplifiers on the tertiary TDM interface, run like stock at 96 kHz with
+ * 32-bit samples in four 32-bit slots; the interface needs the LPASS core
+ * vote of stock "qcom,mi2s-tdm-is-hw-vote-needed". The SM8450 card name
+ * keeps the qcom/sm8450 topology and UCM directories.
+ */
+static const struct qcom_snd_soc_common marble_priv_data = {
+	.driver_name = "sm8450",
+	.dapm_widgets = sc8280xp_dapm_widgets,
+	.num_dapm_widgets = ARRAY_SIZE(sc8280xp_dapm_widgets),
+	.wcd_jack = true,
+	.mi2s_mclk_enable = true,
+	.mi2s_bclk_enable = true,
+	.codec_dai_fmt = SND_SOC_DAIFMT_BC_FC |
+			 SND_SOC_DAIFMT_NB_NF |
+			 SND_SOC_DAIFMT_I2S,
+	.tdm_rate = 96000,
+	.tdm_format = SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S32_LE,
+	.tdm_hw_vote = true,
+};
+
 static const struct qcom_snd_soc_common sm8475_priv_data = {
 	.driver_name = "sm8475",
 	.dapm_widgets = sc8280xp_dapm_widgets,
@@ -576,6 +670,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id snd_sc8280xp_dt_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8550-sndcard", .data = &sm8550_priv_data },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8650-sndcard", .data = &sm8650_priv_data },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8750-sndcard", .data = &sm8750_priv_data },
+	{ .compatible = "xiaomi,marble-sndcard", .data = &marble_priv_data },
 	{}
 };
 
